-<details open><summary>Separate revision analyses are not additive contributions</summary><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Reported analysis, Table 19</th><th class="num">National three-year BI (CAD $000)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Submitted base case</td><td class="num">76,543</td></tr><tr><td>Correction: remove fees, markups and copayments</td><td class="num">73,199</td></tr><tr><td>Population revision alone, after correction</td><td class="num">18,300</td></tr><tr><td>Public-coverage revision alone, after correction</td><td class="num">80,770</td></tr><tr><td>Biologic-growth revision alone, after correction</td><td class="num">87,011</td></tr><tr><td>Switching revision alone, after correction</td><td class="num">27,056</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Correction + all four revisions</strong></td><td class="num"><strong>9,547</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>These separate reanalyses each start after correction; their differences cannot be summed into a national waterfall. Interactions between population, coverage, growth and switching matter. The review could not fully resolve discontinuation, adalimumab dose escalation or subsequent switching because of limitations in the submitted model (pp. 176–177). This page does not claim to reproduce its underlying workbook.</p></details></section>
-<section class="card" id="methods"><div class="eyebrow">12 / Methodology and practical implementation</div><h2>Build an auditable cohort and an auditable counterfactual</h2><div class="grid"><article class="panel"><h3>Case ascertainment</h3><p>Specify index date, lookback, residency, adult age and a common observation window. Define point prevalence at a date or period prevalence over an interval; incident cases require an adequate prior washout. Verify coding versions, diagnostic positions and encounter completeness before applying candidate rules.</p><p>Repeated encounters measure care use, not new people. Link across systems, deduplicate encounters, then count unique patients. Missing diagnoses, delayed diagnosis and misclassification can bias both numerator and eligibility. NACRS non-capture does not prove no emergency care. Codes rarely establish Hurley stage or inadequate response.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Population estimation</h3><p>Top-down approximations and bottom-up records estimate different constructs. Access to care, diagnosis capture, enrollment, indication confirmation and private treatment can all explain disagreement. Validate against sampled charts or registries, report sensitivity and PPV with transportability limitations, and retain alternative definitions.</p><p>Growth in biologic utilization is distinct from population growth or incidence. Do not apply multiple growth factors to the same incoming patients. Keep actively treated patients distinct from historical discontinuers and untreated eligible patients.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Economic interpretation</h3><p>The public perspective includes public costs; patient burden and private payments need separate information. List prices differ from confidential net acquisition costs. State price date, unit, pack size, fees, markups and treatment duration. No rebates are inferred here.</p><p>Induction belongs to new treatment courses, not every established patient every year. Include nonadherence, escalation and discontinuation in transparent scenarios. Annual impact is a flow; cumulative impact is the sum. Round only displayed outputs and identify expected counts versus discrete synthetic people.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Affordability versus value</h3><p>A BIA asks how much a program may spend over a specified horizon under alternative treatment markets. Cost-effectiveness analysis also considers health outcomes relative to costs, often using QALYs and a longer horizon. A favourable BIA does not establish value or comparative effectiveness.</p><p>This counterfactual uses only adalimumab biosimilars as the reference biologic. It excludes broader current-market changes, clinical outcomes, adverse-event costs, background treatment, wound care and service offsets. It is a teaching model, not a decision-ready submission.</p></article></div>
+<section class="card" id="uncertainty"><div class="eyebrow">10 / Uncertainty is part of the result</div><h2>Which assumptions change the decision's financial scale?</h2><div class="toolbar"><label>One-way range ± <input id="tornado-range" type="number" min="1" max="90" step="5" value="25" style="width:80px"> %</label><span class="small">Multiplicative ranges; probabilities bounded to [0,1].</span></div><figure><div id="tornado"></div><figcaption>Each row changes one factor while holding others fixed. Diagnosis and biologic uptake rescale the BIA cohort, representing a top-down interpretation. Their bars are alternatives to changing N, not independent additions. Frequency compares q4w with q2w. A zero discontinuation baseline uses 0 to the selected absolute range.</figcaption></figure><p id="tornado-note"></p><details open><summary>Reproducible Monte Carlo demonstration</summary><p>These distributions are assumed for teaching; they are not fitted to BC records. For a proportion with mean μ and concentration κ, p ~ Beta(μκ, (1−μ)κ). Means at 0 or 1 remain fixed. Positive costs use lognormal factors with cost coefficient of variation (CV) and σ² = log(1 + CV²), log-mean −σ²/2; cohort size uses a mean-one lognormal factor with log-SD 0.2. Independently drawn share values are sorted to preserve increasing uptake, so their marginal distributions are changed by ordering. Other inputs remain fixed.</p><div class="controls"><label class="control">Simulation draws<select id="draws"><option>250</option><option selected>500</option><option>1000</option></select></label><label class="control">Random seed<input id="seed" type="number" min="1" max="4294967295" value="20261019"></label><label class="control">Beta concentration κ<input id="concentration" type="number" min="5" max="1000" value="60"></label><label class="control">Cost coefficient of variation<input id="cv" type="number" min=".01" max="1" step=".01" value=".15"></label></div><button id="run-mc">Run / repeat simulation